QuestBoard:
QuestBoard is a webbased gambified habit and productivitie tracker. It helps users
manage their quests and keep track of their progress while still motivated.

Features: 
- Registration system 
- Login system (sessions)
- Tasks/quests system with timing and reoccurance
- Rewards and levels
- Streaks 
- Ingame store

Installation (via bash): 
- npm install
- npm install promise-mysql
- npm install express-session
- npm install --save-dev vitest
- npm install --save-dev supertest

Database configation: 
{
    "host":     "localhost",
    "user":     "questboard",
    "password": "REDACTED_DEMO_PASSWORD",
    "database": "QuestBoard",
    "multipleStatements": true
}

Database setup:
Run in order on bash: (password = "REDACTED_DEMO_PASSWORD")
- cd sql
- mariadb -u questboard -p QuestBoard < mariadb -u questboard -p < setup.sql   
- mariadb -u questboard -p QuestBoard < ddl.sql
- mariadb -u questboard -p QuestBoard (for next line)
- SET GLOBAL event_scheduler = ON;
- exit;
- mariadb -u questboard -p QuestBoard < functions.sql
- mariadb -u questboard -p QuestBoard < insert.sql   

Running the application:
- node index.js
- open your browser and go to: "http://localhost:1337/QuestBoard"

Vitest: 
- npm test

Smoke test: 
- npm smoke

Manualy test the application: 
- open "http://localhost:1337/QuestBoard"
- you must be redirected to QuestBoard/login
- click on "sign up" to be redirected to QuestBoard/signup
- create an account by entering your name, email and a password that follows the listed conditions
- you will be redirected to QuestBoard/account_created, click on "log in"
- log in by entering the email and password you've just created an account with
- you will be redirected to QuestBoard/dashboard
- click on "create a quest" to be redirected to QuestBoard/quest
- create a quest by filling the form and submiting It
- when redirected to dashboard, complete the quest by clicking on "complete" next to the quest's row on the table "upcoming quests"
- you will get xp and coins
- to know the conditions for the rewards such as how many coins and xps you get and the rules for badges and streaks open 
  "information" from the header
- open your profile by clicking on "profile" to view your information, completed quests and rewards (rewards can also be viewed on 
  the dashboard)
- you can test editing your quest by clicking on "edit" next to the quest on the upcoming quests table in the dashboard and chosing 
  what part you would like to edit
- you can delete a quest by clickig on "delete" next to the quest on the upcoming quests table in the dashboard
- you can change your bio and profile picture from the profile by clicking on the action bottum you wanna do
- open the shop by clicking on "store" in the header
- when redirected to the store, click on "buy" to buy the avatar
- you can view your owned avatars in the profile
- finally, click on "log out" in the header to log out of the session and be redirected to login 

Prototype overview: 

Routing logic: 
- header2 has links to QuestBoard/login & QuestBoard/signup for users before logging in
- /QuestBoard redirects you to QuestBoard/login with no rendering
- /QuestBoard/login is where you log in
- /QuestBoard/signup is where you submit a form and get redirected to /QuestBoard/account_created
- In /QuestBoard/account_created there is a link to QuestBoard/login
- /QuestBoard/dashboard can only be accessed after submitting the log in form in QuestBoard/login
- header links are only accessable after logging in, they are: QuestBoard/profile, QuestBoard/dashboard QuestBoard/store, 
  QuestBoard/information, QuestBoard/logout 
- There are 4 route actions in QuestBoard/dashboard: 
  links: QuestBoard/quest, QuestBoard/profile, QuestBoard/edit_quest, QuestBoard/add_description
  action: QuestBoard/delete_quest which preform a post action and redirects you to QuestBoard/dashboard
- QuestBoard/profile has 4 links: QuestBoard/add_description, QuestBoard/add_birthday, QuestBoard/update_bio, 
  QuestBoard/change_avatar
- QuestBoard/update_bio redirects you back to QuestBoard/profile
- QuestBoard/add_birthday redirects you back to QuestBoard/profile
- QuestBoard/change_avatar redirects you back to QuestBoard/profile
- QuestBoard/add_description redirects you to QuestBoard/dashboard
- QuestBoard/edit_quest has 3 links: QuestBoard/edit_name, QuestBoard/edit_description, QuestBoard/edit_type
- All three links redirect you to QuestBoard/dashboard after submitting the form on them
- QuestBoard info has no links (other than the header links)
- QuestBoard/logout only redirects you to QuestBoard/login and logs you out of the session with no rendering

Registration/ login system functionality: 
- In the datebase there are: inlogging table & profiles table
- Inlogging has email, hashed-password (maneged by bycript) and user-id 
- profiles has other information such as name, birthday, profile picture id ..
- When signing up, app checks if the email is unique and if the password follows conditions, if so, app inserts
  the user information into the databases
- When logging in, app checks if the email and password are ture and logs the user in using session system 
- Edits are made via procedures (for example updating profile picture)

Avatar/ store system:
- In the database there are: store & owned items tables
- store has information on the items the app sells
- owned items has links between the item-id and the user-id who owns the item
- when user buys an item, the app inserts the item id with the user id to the owned items table

Quest system functionality: 
- In the database there are: quests & completed quests tables
- when the user creates a quest, the app links it to the user with user_id and inserts it to the quest_table
- The app sets the due time based off of the quest edit_type
- When completing a quest, the app changes the status of the quest
- The app inserts the quest to the completed quests table
- After midnight (for daily quests) or 7 days after creation time (weekly quests), the app resets the due 
  time via events
- Edits are made via procedures

Streak system: 
- In the database there are: streaks & ongoing streaks tables
- Streaks table has information on the streaks
- Ongoing streaks links the streak id with the user id and the last login date
- When logging in, the app checks the last login date, if it's the same date the app does nothing, if its the 
  very next day, the app adds 1 to the streak, if it's more than a day, the app resets the streak to 1
- When completing a quest, the app checks the status, if it was late, the app resets the streak to 1, if it's 
  early or on time, the app adds 1

Badges: 
- In the database there are: badges, owned badges tables
- Owned badges table links the badge from the badges table to the user id from the profile table
- Users get badges via triggers

Project structure:
QuestBoard/
